course: dictionary
lesson: 7509
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Pottery» is a good example. It can mean the objects, the craft, or the place where they are made.
explain: «Kintsugi is a Japanese art of mending broken pottery with gold.» Here pottery means the objects: the broken pots and bowls. The words broken and mending are your clues.
explain: «Greeks sailed in triremes and traded olive oil, wine and pottery.» Here pottery means things to sell. Ask yourself: does the sentence want a thing, a skill, or a place? That question will often find the meaning for you.
fact: Pottery is pots, bowls, plates and other objects made from clay and baked hard.
fact: Pottery can also mean the craft of making these objects, as in «a pottery class».
fact: A pottery is a place where these objects are made.
fact: A kiln is a very hot oven, and baking clay in it makes the clay hard for good.
fact: «Cracks are common in pottery», but kintsugi shows that a mended crack can be beautiful.
exercise: «Kintsugi is a Japanese art of mending broken pottery with gold.» In this sentence, what is pottery? | The craft of painting pictures | *Pots and bowls made from baked clay | A kind of gold metal | A place where people go to swim
exercise: Ella says, «I'm going to a pottery class on Saturday.» What does pottery mean here? | Pots and plates on a shelf | A place where clay is dug up | A tool for cutting wood | *The craft of making objects from clay
exercise: Potteries are places where clay objects are made. What does potteries mean? | *Places where clay objects are made | People who sell food | Hot ovens for cooking bread | Objects made from clay
test: «Baking clay in a kiln changes it for good.» What does kiln mean? | *A very hot oven | A wheel for shaping pots | A sort of glue | A cold cupboard for clay
test: Mia works in a pottery by the sea. What is a pottery here? | Clay from the riverbank | The craft of mending | Pots and bowls | *A place where pots are made
exam: «Baking clay in a kiln changes its minerals for good, so pottery does not turn back into mud.» What does this tell us? | Clay pots soften again when they get wet | Pottery is always made from mud | *Fired clay objects stay hard and keep their shape | Kilns are cold places for drying clay
